From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mt7915 pci msi for the second hif

The second HIF of the MT7916 took pdev->irq, its legacy INTx.  On the
Airoha AN7563 the INTx of a port does not reach the CPU (the irq is a
dummy shared with the port's PME), so the HIF2 interrupt never fired and
with it the band 1 tx free events and TX status: a station on 5 GHz was
dropped a few seconds after it associated.

Allocate a vector as the main interface does, MSI when there is one.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7915/pci.c
+++ b/mt7915/pci.c
@@ -85,14 +85,24 @@ static struct mt7915_hif *mt7915_pci_ini
 static int mt7915_pci_hif2_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
 	struct mt7915_hif *hif;
+	int ret;
 
 	hif = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*hif), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!hif)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	/*
+	 * MSI when there is one, as for the main interface: a host whose
+	 * legacy INTx does not reach the CPU (Airoha AN7563) left the second
+	 * HIF without interrupts, and with it the band 1 tx free events.
+	 */
+	ret = pci_alloc_irq_vectors(pdev, 1, 1, PCI_IRQ_ALL_TYPES);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
 	hif->dev = &pdev->dev;
 	hif->regs = pcim_iomap_table(pdev)[0];
-	hif->irq = pdev->irq;
+	hif->irq = pci_irq_vector(pdev, 0);
 	spin_lock_bh(&hif_lock);
 	list_add(&hif->list, &hif_list);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&hif_lock);
